<title>USA: Leslie-ADM corn production survey by states.</title>
<headline>Leslie-ADM corn production survey by states.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following tables contain state-by-state corn production estimates published in the Leslie-ADM Investor Services Crop survey.</p>
<p>U.S. CORN PRODUCTION (IN 000'S BUSHELS)</p>
<p>	 LESLIE 11/1/96 USDA 10/1/96  USDA 1995</p>
<p> NEW YORK     78,400	77,700	64,050</p>
<p> PENN	  130,200     129,150	94,080</p>
<p> OHIO	  297,000     297,000     375,100</p>
<p> IND	   681,250     654,000     598,900</p>
<p> ILL	 1,485,000   1,458,000   1,130,000</p>
<p> MICH	  225,600     220,900     249,550</p>
<p> WISC	  348,800     342,400     347,700</p>
<p> MINN	  854,000     819,000     731,850</p>
<p> IOWA	1,736,000   1,674,000   1,402,200</p>
<p> MISSOURI    343,200     332,000     149,940</p>
<p> N DAK	  58,800	58,800	40,290</p>
<p> S DAK	 328,500     328,500     193,550</p>
<p> NEB	 1,208,625   1,179,750     854,700</p>
<p> KANSAS	340,750     340,750     244,280</p>
<p> MARYLAND     59,288	58,590	42,000</p>
<p> VIRGINIA     37,200	37,200	30,525</p>
<p> N.CAROLNA    84,630	81,840	74,900</p>
<p> S.CAROLNA    28,500	28,500	24,115</p>
